(RECEIPTS.--INCOME.--PRODUCE.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The idea covered by the word receipts \(_Einnahme_\) embraces all the new) Tj T*
(additions successively made to one's resources within a given period of) Tj T*
(time.[144-1] Income, on the other hand, embraces only such receipts as) Tj T*
(are the results of economic activity. \(See §§ 2, 11.\) Produce \(_Ertrag_,) Tj T*
(_produit_\) is income, but not from the point of view of the person or) Tj T*
(_subject_ engaged in a business of any kind, but from that of the) Tj T*
(business itself, or of the _object_ with which the business is) Tj T*
(concerned, and on which it, so to speak, acts.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Income is made up of products, the results of labor and of the) Tj T*
(employment and use of resources. These products, the producer may either) Tj T*
(consume himself or exchange against other products, to satisfy a more) Tj T*
(urgent want.[144-2] Hence, spite of the frequency with which we hear) Tj T*
(such expressions as these: "the laborer eats the bread of his employer;") Tj T*
("the capitalist lives by the sweat of the brow of labor;" or, again, a) Tj T*
(manufacturer or business man "lives from the income of his) Tj T*
ET
