(     [Footnote 145-4: In the East, a valuation by one's self of) Tj T*
(     his property is considered a guilty kind of pride, usually) Tj T*
(     punished by the loss of one's possessions. \(_Burckhardt_,) Tj T*
(     Travels in Arabia, I, 72 ff.\) See _Samuel_, 24, on the) Tj T*
(     census made by David. The Egyptians, however, as may be) Tj T*
(     inferred from their monuments, must have very early and very) Tj T*
(     extensively felt the want of some kind of book-keeping such) Tj T*
(     as we have mentioned. A very accurate sort of book-keeping) Tj T*
(     among the more highly cultured Romans, with a daily) Tj T*
(     memorandum and a monthly book with entries from the former) Tj T*
(     \(_adversaria-tabula expensi et accepti_\). Compare _Cicero_,) Tj T*
(     pro Roscio, com. 2, 3; pro Cluent, 30; _Verr._, II, 1, 23,) Tj T*
(     36. The Latin _putare_, from _putus_, pure, means: to make) Tj T*
(     an account clear, and therefore corresponds to the American) Tj T*
(     provincialism, "I reckon," i. e., I believe; and is a) Tj T*
(     remarkable proof of a rigid method of keeping accounts. The) Tj T*
(     Italian, or so-called double-entry method of book-keeping,) Tj T*
(     which gives the most accurate information on the profit from) Tj T*
(     every separate branch of business, became usual among the) Tj T*
(     nations of modern Europe whose civilization was the first to) Tj T*
(     ripen, about the end of the fifteenth century. Its invention) Tj T*
(     is ascribed to the monk Luca Paciolo di Borgo S. Sepolcro.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(     In England, this kind of book-keeping is very gradually) Tj T*
(     coming into use even among farmers, while _Simond_, Voyage) Tj T*
(     en Angleterre, 2 ed., II, 64, _Dunoyer_, Liberté du Travail,) Tj T*
(     VIII, 5, say, "it would in France be considered as) Tj T*
(     ridiculous as the book-keeping of an apple vendor." In) Tj T*
(     Germany, there have been for some time past, manufactories) Tj T*
(     of commercial books. Besides, the remarkable difference) Tj T*
(     brought out by the income tax in England between the exact) Tj T*
(     statements made by large manufacturers, etc., and by those) Tj T*
(     engaged in industry on a medium or small scale, bears) Tj T*
(     evidence of the better way in which the former keep their) Tj T*
(     accounts, the cause and effect of their better business in) Tj T*
(     general. Compare _Knies_, in the Tübing. Zeitschr., 1854,) Tj T*
(     513. On the best mode of determining income, see _Cazaux_,) Tj T*
(     Eléments d'Économie publique et privée, Livre, II. It is) Tj T*
(     especially necessary to keep an account of the increase or) Tj T*
(     diminution, even when accidental, of the value of the fixed) Tj T*
(     capital employed.]) Tj T*
