(SECTION CXLVI.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(NATIONAL INCOME.--ITS STATISTICAL IMPORTANCE.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Among the most important[146-1] but also the most difficult objects of) Tj T*
(statistics, that book-keeping of nations, is national income. In) Tj T*
(estimating it, we may take our starting point from the goods which are) Tj T*
(elements of income, or from the persons who receive them as) Tj T*
(income.[146-2]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In the former case the gross national income consists:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A. Of the raw material newly obtained in the country.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(B. Of imports from foreign countries, including that which is secured by) Tj T*
(piracy, as war-booty, contributions, etc.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
