(Rent is that portion of the regular net product of a piece of land which) Tj T*
(remains after deducting the wages of labor and the interest on the) Tj T*
(capital usual in the country, incorporated into it.[149-1] Hence it is) Tj T*
(the price paid for the using of the land itself, or for what Ricardo) Tj T*
(calls the original inexhaustible forces of the soil which are capable of) Tj T*
(being appropriated.[149-2] This price also depends, of course, on the) Tj T*
(relation between demand and supply; the demand in turn, on the wants and) Tj T*
(means of payment of buyers, but the supply by no means on cost of) Tj T*
(production, which, from the definitions above given, is here) Tj T*
(unthinkable. However, land has this in common with other means of) Tj T*
(production, that its price is mainly determined by that of its products.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
