(cover the cost of production on even the worst soil \(the margin of) Tj T*
(cultivation according to Fawcett\), which must be brought under) Tj T*
(cultivation in order to satisfy the aggregate want. \(See § 110.\) This) Tj T*
(worst land need yield no rent.[150-2] The better land which, with an) Tj T*
(equal outlay of labor and capital, produces a greater yield, furnishes) Tj T*
(an excess over the cost of production.[150-3] This excess is rent,) Tj T*
