(WAGES OF LABOR.--THE MINIMUM OF WAGES.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Human labor cannot, any more than any other commodity, be supplied, in) Tj T*
(the long run, at a price below the cost of production.[161-1] [161-2] The) Tj T*
(cost of production here embraces not only the necessary or customary) Tj T*
(means of subsistence of the workman himself, but also of his family;) Tj T*
(that is, of the coming generation of workmen. The number of the latter) Tj T*
(depends essentially on the demand for labor. If this demand be such that) Tj T*
(it may be satisfied by an average of six children to a family, the rate) Tj T*
(of wages must be such as to support the workman himself and to cover the) Tj T*
(cost of bringing up six children.[161-3] Where it is customary for the) Tj T*
(wife and child, as well as for the father, to work for wages, the father) Tj T*
(does not need to earn the entire support of the family, and hence) Tj T*
(individual wages may be smaller.[161-4] But if it were to fall below the) Tj T*
(cost mentioned above, it would not be long before increased mortality) Tj T*
(and emigration, and a diminution of marriages and births would produce a) Tj T*
(diminution of the supply; the result of which would be, if the demand) Tj T*
(remained the same, a renewed rise of wages.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Conversely, it would be more difficult for the rate of wages to be) Tj T*
(maintained long much above that same cost, in proportion as the) Tj T*
(gratification of the sexual appetite was more generally considered the) Tj T*
(highest pleasure of sense, and the love of parents for their children as) Tj T*
(the most natural human duty. As Adam Smith says, where there is a great) Tj T*
(demand for men, there will always be a large supply of them.[161-5]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(     [Footnote 161-1: Compare _Engel's_ beautiful lecture on the) Tj T*
(     cost of labor to itself \(_Selbstkosten_ = _self-cost_\),) Tj T*
(     Berlin, 1866.]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
