(B. The great economic risk of the work. When a branch of labor necessary) Tj T*
(to a country is, notwithstanding, attended by many chances of failure to) Tj T*
(the individual who devotes himself to it, a sufficient supply of the) Tj T*
(labor can be relied on only in case that the danger attending it is) Tj T*
(compensated for by a corresponding premium paid to success.[168-1] The) Tj T*
(choice of a profession or avocation, Adam Smith has compared to a) Tj T*
(lottery, in which the fortunate winners gain only what the unfortunate) Tj T*
(have lost. The greater the prizes, the greater also the number of) Tj T*
(blanks.[168-2] However, the surplus wages in risky kinds of labor are) Tj T*
(not sufficient to constitute a full insurance premium. This is connected) Tj T*
(with the vanity of men who, as a rule, over-estimate not only their) Tj T*
(talent but their good fortune,[168-3] and especially in youth, when they) Tj T*
(decide on the choice of a profession, etc. According to this, wages must) Tj T*
(be specially low where even complete failure does not endanger the) Tj T*
(living or the social position of the workman. Partly on this account are) Tj T*
(the industries carried on by women so poorly remunerated;[168-4] as also) Tj T*
(such work as is done by a large class of people to fill up their leisure) Tj T*
(hours.[168-5]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The prospect of frequent interruptions in any kind of labor must have) Tj T*
(the same effect on the wages paid for it as its economic or business) Tj T*
(risk.[168-6] Thus, for instance, a mason or roofer must earn at least) Tj T*
(enough, during the days he can work, to enable him to live during the) Tj T*
(time he is prevented working by bad weather. Hence, the highness of his) Tj T*
(wages may, in some respects, be called an apparent one.[168-7] Wages) Tj T*
(paid by the week more generally tend to equality than wages paid by the) Tj T*
(day, and more so yet wages paid by the year, for then winter and summer) Tj T*
(compensate the one for the other. When the workman must be ever ready to) Tj T*
(perform his task, account must be taken not only of the number of hours) Tj T*
(he is engaged, but also of fractions of his waiting hours, which must be) Tj T*
