(A permanently[173-1] high rate of wages[173-2] is, both as cause and) Tj T*
(effect, very intimately connected with a flourishing condition of) Tj T*
(national life. It proves on the one hand, great productiveness of the) Tj T*
(public economy of the people generally: prudence, self-respect and) Tj T*
(self-control, even of the lowest classes, virtues, which, however, are) Tj T*
(found, on the whole, only where political liberty exists, and where the) Tj T*
(lowest classes are rightly valued by the higher.[173-3] On the other) Tj T*
(hand, it produces a condition of the great majority of that portion of) Tj T*
(the population who have to support themselves on the wages they receive,) Tj T*
(worthy of human beings, a condition in which they can educate their) Tj T*
(children, enjoy the present and provide for the future. Equality before) Tj T*
(the law and participation in the affairs of government are empty) Tj T*
(phrases, and even tend to inflame the passions, where the rate of wages) Tj T*
(is not high. When the lower classes are dissatisfied, in highly) Tj T*
(civilized countries, with the sensitiveness and mobility of the whole) Tj T*
(national life, there can be no certainty of the freedom of the middle) Tj T*
(classes or of the rule of the upper. Here, in other respects, also, the) Tj T*
(philanthropy of employers harmonizes remarkably well with their) Tj T*
(reasonable self-interest. According to § 40, only the well-paid workman) Tj T*
(can accomplish anything really good, just as, conversely, only the good) Tj T*
(workman is on the whole, and in the long run, well paid. This suggests) Tj T*
(the physiological law, that where muscular activity is great, nutrition) Tj T*
(must be great, likewise; and the rapid waste and repair of tissues) Tj T*
(strengthens the muscles and gives tone to the whole physical life. With) Tj T*
