(When, circumstances being otherwise unaltered, the aggregate income of a) Tj T*
(nation decreases, the wages of labor are wont to be lower in proportion) Tj T*
(as the points above mentioned, and which are unfavorable to the laborer) Tj T*
(in his competition, appear.[174-1] The worse distribution, also, of the) Tj T*
(national resources, when, instead of a numerous middle class, a few) Tj T*
(over-rich people monopolize all that is to be possessed, diminishes the) Tj T*
(wages of common labor and thus again produces a worse distribution than) Tj T*
(before.[174-2] In a similar way, wages must decline when the mode of) Tj T*
(life of the laboring class, or the quality of their work, has) Tj T*
(deteriorated. Some of these causes may exist transitorily even among) Tj T*
(otherwise flourishing nations; as, for instance, in war times,[174-3] or) Tj T*
(when population for a while grows more rapidly than national wealth. But) Tj T*
(among nations universally declining, they are all wont to meet, and one) Tj T*
(strengthens the other.[174-4] One of the saddest symptoms of such a) Tj T*
(condition is the low value here put upon the life and strength of) Tj T*
(workmen. The cheapness of labor has indeed a charm for enterprising) Tj T*
(spirits, which induces them to employ human labor even where machinery,) Tj T*
(beasts, etc., would economically be better adapted to the performance of) Tj T*
(the work.[174-5] Day-laborers are, on this account, more profitable to) Tj T*
(persons of enterprise \(_Unternehmer_=_undertaker_\) because they can more) Tj T*
(easily rid themselves of them. But such egotistic calculation should) Tj T*
(have no place even in the case of actual slaves.[174-6]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Besides, it not unfrequently happens, that the laboring class seek to) Tj T*
(oppose the decline of wages by increasing their industry, shortening) Tj T*
(their holidays and leisure, and by drawing their wives and children into) Tj T*
(their work. This may, under certain circumstances, result in an increase) Tj T*
(of the national income, and thus constitute a transition to the) Tj T*
(restoration of high wages, especially if beforehand there was reason to) Tj T*
(complain of the idleness of the working class. But if the other) Tj T*
(circumstances of competition are unfavorable to the working class, if) Tj T*
(especially they used their personally increased income to add to the) Tj T*
(population, it would not be long before they fell back to their previous) Tj T*
(state. In such case, the consequence is, that the same quantity of labor) Tj T*
(has become cheaper; that all permanent profit falls to the capitalists) Tj T*
(and landowners, and all that remains to the laboring class is only) Tj T*
(greater toil, a sadder home-life, and sadder children. The danger of) Tj T*
(such an issue is all the greater, because few things so much contribute) Tj T*
(to reckless marriages and the thoughtless procreation of children, as) Tj T*
