(Within the limits of the same national-economic territory, the different) Tj T*
(employments of capital tend uniformly to pay the same rate of) Tj T*
(interest.[180-1] If one branch of business were much more profitable) Tj T*
(than another, it would be to the interest of the owners of capital to) Tj T*
(allow it to flow into the former and out of the latter, until a level) Tj T*
(was reached.[180-2]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The most noticeable exception to this rule is only an apparent one. The) Tj T*
(revenue \(_Nutzung_\) derived from the use of capital must not be) Tj T*
(confounded with its partial restoration.[180-3] Thus, for instance, the) Tj T*
(rent of a house, if the entire capital is not to be sooner or later) Tj T*
(consumed entirely, must embrace, besides a payment for the use of the) Tj T*
(house, a sum sufficient to defray the expenses of repairing it, and even) Tj T*
(to effect a gradual accumulation of capital for the purpose of) Tj T*
(rebuilding. The risk attending the investment of capital plays a very) Tj T*
(large part and must be taken into special consideration. If the risk in) Tj T*
(a business be so great that ten who engage in it succeed and ten fail,) Tj T*
(the returns of the former, which are more than double those usual in the) Tj T*
(country, in reality pay, when the ten who failed are taken into the) Tj T*
(account, only the rate of interest customary in the country. The risk) Tj T*
(may depend on the uncertainty of the person to whom the capital is) Tj T*
(confided;[180-4] on the uncertainty of the branch of business in which) Tj T*
(it is intended to employ it,[180-5] or on the uncertainty of the) Tj T*
(commercial situation in general; but especially may it depend on the) Tj T*
(uncertainty of the laws.[180-6] The temporary lying idle of capital, for) Tj T*
(instance, in dwelling houses at bathing places during the winter season,) Tj T*
(increases the rate of interest much more than it does the rate of wages) Tj T*
(in the corresponding case of the lying idle of labor; for the reason) Tj T*
(that there is something pleasurable in the repose of the latter.) Tj T*
(\(_Senior._\) On the whole, the vanity of mankind has an effect upon the) Tj T*
(rate of interest similar to that which it has on the rate of wages. \(See) Tj T*
(§ 168.\) It causes the small chances of loss to be estimated below their) Tj T*
(real value, and the extraordinary chances of gain above it.[180-7]) Tj T*
