(seldom made. To make such loans would be to run too many risks; risks) Tj T*
(through a want of knowledge of persons or circumstances, on account of) Tj T*
(the difficulties in the way of continued supervision, and of being able) Tj T*
(to assert and defend one's rights away from home.[187-5] Loans are much) Tj T*
(more readily made to foreign states, to great corporations, or) Tj T*
(joint-stock companies, whose condition is well-known; and which, by) Tj T*
(reason of their perpetuity, have a deep and obvious interest in) Tj T*
(maintaining an honorable reputation. The issuing of certificates of) Tj T*
(stock, etc., has greatly facilitated international trade in) Tj T*
(capital.[187-6] But the mode of loaning in foreign parts preferred is to) Tj T*
(sell them commodities, and to require payment for them only after some) Tj T*
(time has elapsed, of course, with interest. Purchases, on the contrary,) Tj T*
(are paid for immediately, possibly even in advance.[187-7] The lower the) Tj T*
(rate of interest in a country is, the longer and more cheaply can it) Tj T*
(give credit to others; a new reason why the less civilized countries are) Tj T*
(particularly fond of trading with the most civilized.[187-8] [187-9]) Tj T*
