(Beneficial as the spur of a low rate of interest is for countries) Tj T*
(capable of development, it is a heavy drag on a stationary people, and) Tj T*
(more so on those who have lost a portion of the field for the investment) Tj T*
(of their capital by the competition of too powerful rivals.[188-1] A) Tj T*
(real superabundance of capital is attended with cares and temptations) Tj T*
(for the middle classes very similar to those caused by a so-called) Tj T*
(over-population, especially to dishonesty and extravagance.[188-2] When) Tj T*
(capital, population and the skillfulness of labor remaining the same,) Tj T*
(continues to increase, the enlarged capital may very readily have every) Tj T*
(succeeding year only the same return to divide among its owners, that) Tj T*
(the smaller had in previous years.[188-3] Hence additional saving here) Tj T*
(would produce no real enrichment of the people; and it might even happen) Tj T*
(that the instinct to accumulate capital might in the future become) Tj T*
(torpid to a greater degree than the capital itself had increased. In any) Tj T*
(case, however, the decline of the rate of interest can continue only to) Tj T*
(a certain point. There are numberless persons who would rather consume) Tj T*
(their capital, or invest it in hazardous speculations than put it out at) Tj T*
(interest at one per cent. a year.[188-4] At least, the tendency of a) Tj T*
(decline in the rate of interest is, in the case of the richer, to) Tj T*
(increase the amount of capital consumed as compared with productive) Tj T*
(capital. The more moderate, sober and provident a people are, the lower) Tj T*
(may the rate of interest decline without producing this effect. And so,) Tj T*
(the more the capital of a nation is concentrated in the hands of a few;) Tj T*
(because then the owners of capital are all the later forced to break in) Tj T*
(upon it, for the sake of subsistence.[188-5] [188-6]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Among nations which have totally declined, the rate of interest is wont) Tj T*
(to reach a high point once more; the natural result of great losses of) Tj T*
(capital and men, while, at the same time, the freedom of the lower) Tj T*
(classes and the security of property have been either curtailed or lost.) Tj T*
(The weakness of age is, in many respects, even in the case of nations, a) Tj T*
(second childhood.[188-7]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
