(redemption, by which the debtor gave his creditor the use and enjoyment) Tj T*
(of a piece of land a sort of interest in kind, but which he could at any) Tj T*
(time recover back, by payment of the principal. This was not very) Tj T*
(oppressive on the debtor, as he was the only party who could recall the) Tj T*
(contract.[191-5] In a higher stage of civilization, indeed the) Tj T*
(continuance of this species of land-pledge would be exceedingly) Tj T*
(disadvantageous, since the momentary possessor of a piece of land which) Tj T*
