(INTEREST-POLICY.--GOVERNMENT INTERFERENCE.--FIXED RATES.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Instead of the medieval prohibition of interest, most modern states have) Tj T*
(established fixed rates of interest, the exceeding or evasion of which,) Tj T*
(by contract or otherwise, is declared null and void, and is usually) Tj T*
(punishable as usury.[192-1] If the fixing of the rate is intended to) Tj T*
(depress the rate of interest customary in the country,[192-2] [192-3] it) Tj T*
(uniformly fails of its object. If control were great enough, vigilant) Tj T*
(and rigid enough, which is scarcely imaginable, to prevent all) Tj T*
