(should take great care, lest by an incautious framing of its laws, it) Tj T*
(should put judges in such a position that they may be compelled to) Tj T*
(coöperate in the execution of immoral contracts.[194-2] In the lowest) Tj T*
(strata, so to speak, of the loaning business, the medieval condition) Tj T*
(continues to exist \(§ 190\) after it has disappeared in the upper. Here,) Tj T*
(the loan is effected scarcely ever for the purposes of production, but) Tj T*
(most generally because of the most urgent necessity; and the debtor is) Tj T*
(not in a condition, from want of education, and especially from his) Tj T*
(ignorance of arithmetic, to estimate the magnitude of the burthen he has) Tj T*
(undertaken. The business of loaning is, under such circumstances,) Tj T*
(considered dishonorable, to some extent, by the public. And when a) Tj T*
(business necessary in itself is held disreputable by public opinion, the) Tj T*
(usual result is that bad men alone engage in it.[194-3] Real competition) Tj T*
(which would but fix the natural price is wanting here in proportion as) Tj T*
(the debtor is anxious for secrecy.[194-4]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
