(the word, the abolition of or the doing away with an utility without any) Tj T*
(regard to the question whether another higher utility takes its place;) Tj T*
(in its narrower sense \(consumption proper\), a decrease of resources of) Tj T*
(any kind. Consumption is the counterpart of production \(§ 30\), the top) Tj T*
(of the tree of which production is the roots, and the circulation and) Tj T*
(distribution of goods the trunk. \(_A. Walker._\) There is, also, what) Tj T*
(Riedel calls immaterial consumption, as when a utility disappears,) Tj T*
