(The commonest kind of consumption is that caused by the use of a thing,) Tj T*
(or by the employing of it for the purpose of acquisition or of) Tj T*
(enjoyment.[207-1] From time immemorial, enjoyment-consumption has been,) Tj T*
(preponderantly, the affair of women, as acquisition-consumption has been) Tj T*
(the business of men.[207-2] Other circumstances being equal, the degree) Tj T*
(or extent of consumption by use \(use-consumption\) is determined by) Tj T*
(national character. Thus, for instance, the cleanliness and love of) Tj T*
(order characteristic of the Dutch have contributed greatly to the long) Tj T*
(preservation in good condition of their dwellings and household) Tj T*
(articles.[207-3]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In the higher stages of civilization, the use of goods is wont to be) Tj T*
(divided more and more into special branches, according to the different) Tj T*
(peculiarities of the goods themselves, and of the different wants of) Tj T*
(men; a course of things which is, both as cause and effect, intimately) Tj T*
(related to the division of labor. I here speak of a principle of) Tj T*
(_division of use_ \(differentiation and specialization\). Thus, for) Tj T*
(instance, Lorenz Lange, in 1722, found only one kind of tea in the trade) Tj T*
(between Russia and China; Müller, in 1750, found seven; Pallas, in 1772,) Tj T*
(ten; and Erman, in 1829, about seven hundred.[207-4] As the number of) Tj T*
(gradations of different kinds of the same goods increases with) Tj T*
(civilization, there is, in times of war, a retrogression in this) Tj T*
(respect, to a lower economic stage.[207-5]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Opposed to this, we have the principle of the combination of use. There) Tj T*
(are numberless kinds of goods which may serve a great many just as well) Tj T*
(as they can one exclusive user; and this either successively or) Tj T*
(simultaneously, inasmuch as there is no necessity why, with the) Tj T*
(increasing use of the object, the size of the object itself should) Tj T*
(increase in an equal proportion. \(According to Marlo: wealth usable by) Tj T*
(one; wealth usable by many; wealth usable by all.\) Thus, for instance, a) Tj T*
(public library may be incomparably more complete, and accessible in a) Tj T*
(still higher degree than ten private libraries which together cost as) Tj T*
(much as it did. And so, a restaurant-keeper may serve a hundred guests) Tj T*
(at the same time, with a much greater table-variety, more to their) Tj T*
(taste, and at a more convenient time, than if each person made the same) Tj T*
(outlay for his private kitchen.[207-6] While formerly, only the great) Tj T*
(could travel rapidly, combination of use has enabled even the lower) Tj T*
