(The least enjoyable of all consumption \(_loss-consumption_\) is that) Tj T*
(which is the work of nature; and nature is certainly most consuming in) Tj T*
(the tropics. During the rainy season, in the region of the upper Ganges,) Tj T*
(mushrooms shoot up in every corner of the houses; books on shelves swell) Tj T*
(to such an extent that three occupy the place previously occupied by) Tj T*
(four; those left on the table get covered over with a coat of moss) Tj T*
(one-eighth of an inch in thickness. The saltpetre that gathers on the) Tj T*
(walls has to be removed every week in baskets, to keep it from eating) Tj T*
(into the bricks. Numberless moths devour the clothing. Schomburgk found) Tj T*
(that, in Guiana, iron instruments which lay on the ground during the) Tj T*
(rainy season became entirely useless within a few days, that silver) Tj T*
(coins oxydized, etc.; evidently a great obstacle in the way of the) Tj T*
(employment of machinery. In summer, the soil of this same region, so) Tj T*
(rich in roots, is so parched by the heat, that subterranean fires) Tj T*
(sometimes cause the most frightful destruction.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
