(SECTION CCX.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(NECESSITY OF CONSIDERING WHAT IS REALLY CONSUMED.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Whenever there is question of consumption, it is necessary to examine) Tj T*
(with rigid scrutiny, what it is that has been really consumed; that is,) Tj T*
(that has lost in utility. The person, for instance, who pays twenty) Tj T*
(dollars for a coat, has consumed that amount of capital only when the) Tj T*
(coat has been worn out.[210-1] What is called the consumption of one's) Tj T*
(income in advance is nothing but the consumption of a portion of capital) Tj T*
(which the consuming party intends to make good from his future) Tj T*
(income.[210-2] Fixed capital, too, can certainly be directly consumed;) Tj T*
(for instance, when the owner of a house treats the entire rent he) Tj T*
(receives from it as net income, makes no repairs, and no savings to put) Tj T*
(up a new building at some future time. As a rule, however, the owner of) Tj T*
(fixed capital must, in order to consume it, first exchange it against) Tj T*
(circulating capital. Thus the prodigality and dissipation, especially of) Tj T*
(courts of absolute princes, have found numerous defenders who have) Tj T*
(claimed that they are uninjurious, provided only the money spent in) Tj T*
(extravagance remained in the country.[210-3] The prodigality itself,) Tj T*
(that is, the unnecessary destruction of wealth is not, on that account,) Tj T*
(any the less disastrous.[210-4] If, for instance, there are fire-works) Tj T*
(to the amount of 10,000 dollars, manufactured exclusively by the workmen) Tj T*
(of the country, ordered for a gala day; the night before they are used) Tj T*
(for purposes of display, the national wealth embraces two separate) Tj T*
(amounts, aggregating 20,000 dollars; that is, 10,000 dollars in silver) Tj T*
(and 10,000 in rockets, etc. The day after, the 10,000 in silver are) Tj T*
(indeed still in existence, but of the 10,000 in rockets, etc., there is) Tj T*
(nothing left. If the order had been made from a foreign country the) Tj T*
(reverse would have been the case, the silver stores of the people would) Tj T*
(have been diminished, but their supply of powder would remain intact.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In a similar way, there is occasion given for the greatest) Tj T*
(misunderstanding when people so frequently speak of producers and) Tj T*
(consumers as if they were two different classes of people. Every man is) Tj T*
(a consumer of many kinds of goods; but, at the same time, he is a) Tj T*
(producer, unless he be a child, an invalid, a robber, a pick-pocket,) Tj T*
(etc.[210-5] At the same time, Bastiat is right in saying that in case of) Tj T*
(doubt when the interests of production and of consumption come in) Tj T*
(conflict, the state, as the representative of the aggregate interest,) Tj T*
(should range itself on the side of the latter. If we carry things on) Tj T*
(both sides to their extremest consequences, the self-seeking desire of) Tj T*
(consumers would lead to the utmost cheapness, that is, to universal) Tj T*
(superfluity, and the self-seeking wish of producers to the utmost) Tj T*
(dearness, that is, to universal want.[210-6]) Tj T*
