(There is no production possible without consumption. The embodiment of a) Tj T*
(special utility into any substance is a limitation of its general) Tj T*
(utility. Thus, for instance, when corn is baked into bread, it can no) Tj T*
(longer be used for the manufacture of brandy or of starch.[211-1]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(When, therefore, consumption is a condition \(outlay\) to production it is) Tj T*
(called productive \(reproductive\).[211-2] Here, indeed, the form of the) Tj T*
(consumed goods is destroyed, but the value of the goods lives on in the) Tj T*
(new product.) Tj T*
