(invention!" Leaving mere animals out of consideration,[213-3] those men) Tj T*
(who experience very few wants, with the exception of some rare and) Tj T*
(highly intellectual natures, prefer rest to labor. Therefore, when) Tj T*
(European merchants desire to engage in trade with a savage nation they) Tj T*
(have uniformly to begin by sending them their nails, axes,) Tj T*
(looking-glasses, brandy, etc., as gifts. Not until the savage has) Tj T*
(experienced a new enjoyment does the want of continuing it make itself) Tj T*
(felt; or is he prepared to produce for purposes of commerce.[213-4] In a) Tj T*
