(maxim: _Si quem volueris esse divitem, non est quod augeas divitias, sed) Tj T*
(minuas cupiditates \(Seneca\)_, would, if consistently carried out, have) Tj T*
(thwarted the advance of civilization and frustrated the improvement of) Tj T*
(man's condition. On the other hand, most political economists, without) Tj T*
(more ado, assume that individuals, and still more nations, are wont to) Tj T*
(extend the aggregate of their enjoyments just as far as there is a) Tj T*
(possibility of satisfying their wants. But they forget here how great a) Tj T*
(part is played in the world, as men are constituted, by the principle of) Tj T*
(inertia.[214-2] At the first blush, what seems more natural than that) Tj T*
(the less labor a people need employ to obtain the most indispensable) Tj T*
(means of subsistence, the more time and taste would remain to them to) Tj T*
(satisfy their more refined wants. According to this, we should expect to) Tj T*
(discover a more refined civilization, especially, in intellectual) Tj T*
(matters, in the earliest periods, when population is small, when land) Tj T*
(exists in excess and is not yet exhausted. But, in reality, precisely) Tj T*
(the reverse is the case. In the earliest stages of civilization) Tj T*
(accessible to our observation, we find materialism prevailing in its) Tj T*
(coarsest form, and life absorbed entirely by the lowest physical wants.) Tj T*
