(Hence, one of the most essential conditions of a prosperous national) Tj T*
(economy is that the development of consumption should keep equal pace) Tj T*
(with that of production, and supply with demand.[215-1] The growth of a) Tj T*
(nation's economy naturally depends on this: that production should) Tj T*
(always be, so to speak, one step in advance of consumption, just as the) Tj T*
(organism of the animal body grows from the fact that the secretions) Tj T*
(always amount to something less than the amount of additional nutrition.) Tj T*
(A preponderance of secretions would here be disease; but so would be a) Tj T*
(too great preponderance of nutrition. Now, the politico-economical) Tj T*
(disease which is produced by the lagging behind of consumption and by) Tj T*
(the supply being much in advance of the demand, is called a commercial) Tj T*
(\(market\) crisis. Its immediate consequence is, that for a great many) Tj T*
(commodities produced, no purchasers can be found. The effect of this is) Tj T*
(naturally to lower prices. The profit of capital and wages diminish. A) Tj T*
(transition into another branch of production, not overcrowded, is either) Tj T*
(not possible at all or is attended with care, great difficulties and) Tj T*
(loss. It is very seldom that all these disadvantages are confined to the) Tj T*
(one branch in which the disease had its original seat. For, since the) Tj T*
(resources of the one class of producers have diminished, they cannot) Tj T*
(purchase as much from others as usual. The most distant members of the) Tj T*
(politico-economic body may be thereby affected.[215-2]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
