(Lastly, the mere introduction of trade by money destroys as it were the) Tj T*
(use of the whole abstract theory.[217-5] So long as original barter) Tj T*
(prevailed, supply and demand met face to face. But by the intervention) Tj T*
(of money, the seller is placed in a condition to purchase only after a) Tj T*
(time, that is, to postpone the other half of the exchange-transaction as) Tj T*
(he wishes. Hence it follows that supply does not necessarily produce a) Tj T*
(corresponding demand in the real market. And thus a general crisis may) Tj T*
(be produced, especially by a sudden diminution of the medium of) Tj T*
(circulation.[217-6] And so, many very abundant harvests, which have) Tj T*
(produced a great decline in the value of raw material, and no less so a) Tj T*
(too large fixation of capital which stops before its completion,[217-7]) Tj T*
(may lead to general over-production. In a word, production does not) Tj T*
(always carry with itself the guaranty that it shall find a proper) Tj T*
(market, but only when it is developed in all directions, where it is) Tj T*
(progressive and in harmony with the whole national economy. To use) Tj T*
(Michel Chevalier's expression, the saliant angles of the one-half must) Tj T*
(correspond to the re-entrant angles of the other, or confusion will) Tj T*
(reign everywhere. Even in individual industrial enterprises, the proper) Tj T*
(combination of the different kinds of labor employed in them is an) Tj T*
(indispensable condition of success. Let us suppose a factory in which) Tj T*
(there are separate workmen occupied with nothing but the manufacture of) Tj T*
(ramrods. If these now exceed the proper limits of their production and) Tj T*
(have manufactured perhaps ten times as many ramrods as can be used in a) Tj T*
(year, can their colleagues, employed in the making of the locks or) Tj T*
(butt-ends of the gun, profit by their outlay? Scarcely. There will be a) Tj T*
(stagnation of the entire business, because part of its capital is) Tj T*
(paralyzed, and all the workmen will suffer damage.[217-8] [217-9]) Tj T*
