(During the middle ages, industry and commerce had made as yet but little) Tj T*
(progress. Hence it was as difficult then for luxury to be ministered to) Tj T*
(by fine furniture as by the products of foreign countries. Individual) Tj T*
(ornamental pieces, especially arms and drinking cups,[225-1] were wont) Tj T*
(to be the only articles of luxury. We have inventories of the domains of) Tj T*
