(linen owned were two bed-sheets, a table-cloth and a pocket) Tj T*
(handkerchief.[225-2] Fashion is here very constant; because clothing was) Tj T*
(comparatively dearer than at present. And so now in the East. In the) Tj T*
(matter of dwellings, too, more regard was had to size and durability,) Tj T*
(than to elegance and convenience. The palaces of Alfred the Great were) Tj T*
(so frailly built that the walls had to be covered with curtains as a) Tj T*
(protection against the wind, and the lights to be inclosed in) Tj T*
(lanterns.[225-3]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Hence the disposition to use the products of the home soil as articles) Tj T*
