(The change in this situation takes place first of all in the churches) Tj T*
(and in the cities. The Church has passed through almost every stage of) Tj T*
(development in advance of the State; and civilization, both in the good) Tj T*
(and bad sense of the term, has become general, and gradually acclimated) Tj T*
(in the rural districts, through the influence of the cities. In the) Tj T*
(Church, the earliest art endeavored to reach the beautiful. There, we) Tj T*
(first find music, painting, sculpture, foreign perfumes, incense and) Tj T*
(variegated garments.[227-1] In the cities, growing industry introduces a) Tj T*
(more attractive style of clothing and a more ornamental style of) Tj T*
(household furniture. Commerce, beginning to thrive, raises foreign) Tj T*
(commodities into wants,[227-2] and thus the old luxury of feudal times) Tj T*
(is modified.[227-3] The large number of idle servants is diminished. All) Tj T*
(the more refined pleasures are extended downward to wider circles of the) Tj T*
(people. Instead of individual bards, rhapsodists, skalds and) Tj T*
(minnesingers, we have the beginnings of the theater, and instead of) Tj T*
(tournaments, the shooting matches. \(_Freischiessen._\)) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(But it is remarkable how much earlier here pomp and splendor are) Tj T*
(considered than convenience. The Spanish _romanceros_ of the 12th) Tj T*
(century display wonderful splendor in their descriptions of the Cid, and) Tj T*
(the trousseau of his daughters. But, on the other hand, the wife of) Tj T*
(Charles VII. seems to have been the only French woman in the 15th) Tj T*
(century who had more than two linen chemises. Even in the 16th century,) Tj T*
(it frequently happened that a princess made a present to a prince of a) Tj T*
(single shirt. At this time the German middle class were wont to sleep) Tj T*
(naked.[227-4]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
