(The direction which luxury takes in times when civilization is advanced,) Tj T*
(is towards the real, healthy and tasteful enjoyment of life, rather than) Tj T*
(an inconvenient display. This tendency is exceedingly well expressed by) Tj T*
(the English word _comfort_, and it is in modern England that the luxury) Tj T*
(of the second period has found it happiest development. It is found side) Tj T*
(by side with frugality; and it frequently even looks like a return to) Tj T*
(the unaffected love of nature.[228-1]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Thus, since Rousseau's time,[228-2] the so-called English gardens have) Tj T*
