(The whole social character of this luxury has something) Tj T*
(equalizing[230-1] in it; but it supposes particularly that there is not) Tj T*
(too marked a difference in the resources of the people.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A proper gradation of national wants is best guarantied by a good) Tj T*
(distribution of the national resources.[230-2] The more unequal the) Tj T*
(latter is, the more is there spent on vain wants instead of on real) Tj T*
(ones; and the more numerous are the instances of rapid and even immoral) Tj T*
(consumption. Where there are only a few over-rich men, more foreign) Tj T*
(products and products of capital are wont to be called for than home) Tj T*
(products and productions of labor; and luxury especially despises all) Tj T*
(those commodities manufactured in large institutions.[230-3] Every) Tj T*
(change in the consumption-customs of a people, in this respect, should) Tj T*
(be most carefully observed; thus, for instance, whether brandy is) Tj T*
(exchanged for beer, tobacco for meat, cotton for cloth, or the) Tj T*
(reverse.[230-4]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(One of the characteristics of this period is the endeavor to possess the) Tj T*
(best quality of whatever is possessed at all, and to be satisfied with) Tj T*
(less of it rather than purchase more of an inferior quality. This is,) Tj T*
(essentially, to practice frugality, inasmuch as certain) Tj T*
(production-services remain the same whether the commodity is of the best) Tj T*
(or the worst quality, and that commodities of the best quality are more) Tj T*
(superior to the worst in intrinsic goodness than they are in price. But) Tj T*
(this course supposes a certain well-being already existing.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In this period, also, the luxury of the state is wont to take the) Tj T*
(direction of those enjoyments which are accessible to all.[230-5]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
