(The idea of societies for mutual assistance intended to divide the loss) Tj T*
(caused by destructive accidents which one person would not be able to) Tj T*
(recover from among a great many is very ancient. The insurance of their) Tj T*
(members against causes of impoverishment was one of the principal) Tj T*
(elements[237-1] of the strength of the medieval communities \(_Gemeinden) Tj T*
(und Körperschaften._\) If we compare these insurance institutions of the) Tj T*
(middle ages with those of the present, we discover the well-known) Tj T*
(difference between a _corporation_ and an _association_. There the) Tj T*
(members stand to one another in the relation of _persons_ who,) Tj T*
(therefore, seek to guaranty their entire life in the one combination;) Tj T*
(here, they appear only as the representatives of limited portions of) Tj T*
(capital confronted with a definite risk, the average of which may be) Tj T*
(accurately determined. Hence, the former are of small extent, mostly) Tj T*
(local; the latter may extend over whole continents, and even over the) Tj T*
(whole earth. The former have uniformly equal members; the latter embrace) Tj T*
(men of the most different classes. While the former, therefore, simply) Tj T*
(govern themselves, often only on the occasion of their festive) Tj T*
(gatherings, the latter need a precise charter, an artificial tariff and) Tj T*
(a board of officers.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(As the absolute monarchical police-state constitutes, generally, the) Tj T*
(bridge between the middle ages and modern times, so too the transition) Tj T*
(from the medieval to the modern system of insurance has been frequently) Tj T*
(introduced by state insurance.[237-2] [237-3] This was very natural at a) Tj T*
(time when the guilds of the middle ages had lost their importance, and) Tj T*
(private industry was not ripe enough to supply the void left by them.) Tj T*
(The government of a country, far in advance intellectually of the) Tj T*
(majority of its subjects, may, by force, induce them to participate in) Tj T*
(the beneficent effects of insurance, and immediately provide) Tj T*
(institutions extensive enough to guaranty real safety. While it may be) Tj T*
(called a rule that mature private industry satisfies wants more rapidly,) Tj T*
(in greater variety, and more cheaply than state industry; in the case of) Tj T*
