(So far as security is concerned, no absolute preference can be accorded) Tj T*
(to either of these classes. Mutual insurance companies require to extend) Tj T*
(their business very largely[237a-2] to be able to meet great damage. And) Tj T*
(even where the liability of the members is unlimited, care must be taken) Tj T*
(to distinguish between the legally and the actually possible.[237a-3]) Tj T*
(The joint capital of a well organized[237a-4] premium-association) Tj T*
(affords, in this respect sufficient security from the first, but the) Tj T*
(ratio between its security-fund and the amount of its assumed) Tj T*
(liabilities becomes less favorable as the business is extended, in case) Tj T*
(the fund itself is not enlarged.[237a-5] Mutual insurance may accomplish) Tj T*
(something analogous to that accomplished by a joint-stock fund by) Tj T*
(collecting a reserve of yearly dues in advance, thus modifying the) Tj T*
(burdensome vacillation of the amount payable each year.[237a-6]) Tj T*
(Experience, however, teaches, that the strongest form of mutual) Tj T*
(insurance, that supported either by municipalities or by the state, has) Tj T*
(been able to meet extraordinary damage from fire much better than) Tj T*
(premium-institutions, which are too quickly left in the lurch by the) Tj T*
(stockholders when the damage is greater than the amount of the stock) Tj T*
(subscribed. So also loss from fire caused by war or riots is for the) Tj T*
(most part and on principle, excluded by speculative insurance) Tj T*
(institutions.[237a-7]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In point of cheapness to the insured, mutual insurance seems to have the) Tj T*
(advantage, since it contemplates no profit.[237a-8] From a) Tj T*
(national-economical point of view, also, it is very much of a question,) Tj T*
(whether the active competition of premium institutions, in a sphere) Tj T*
(which affords little room for industry proper, is more of a spur to make) Tj T*
(them "puff up" their claims \(_Reclamen_\) or to the simplification of) Tj T*
(their administration.[237a-9] However, premium-institutions are more) Tj T*
(easily capable of extending the circle of their business;[237a-10] which) Tj T*
(of itself decreases the general expenses and strengthens their insuring) Tj T*
(power. Premium-insurance supposes a greater development of capitalistic) Tj T*
(speculation than does mutual insurance. But, even in the highest stages) Tj T*
(of civilization, the competition of some mutual insurance companies is) Tj T*
(desirable to protect the insured from a too high rate of profit to the) Tj T*
(insurers.[237a-11] [237a-12] And since the principle of mutual insurance) Tj T*
(has so little attraction for capitalists in a time like that in which we) Tj T*
(live that it can be maintained perhaps only by the support of the state) Tj T*
(or of municipalities, we may consider the desirableness of the state's) Tj T*
(continuing to participate in some way in the matter of insurance as) Tj T*
(established.) Tj T*
