() Tj T*
(The present system of fire insurance has been introduced in many places by) Tj T*
(the establishment of so-called domanial fire-guilds \(_Domanial-Brandgilden_\),) Tj T*
(by which the country population on crown-lands bound themselves to mutually) Tj T*
(assist one another by furnishing thatch, and horse and hand power in the) Tj T*
(rebuilding of burned houses. Whatever was wanting after this was made up by) Tj T*
(gratuitous supplies of wood from the public forests, by the granting of) Tj T*
(governmental fire-licenses to beg \(_begging letters_\), by permission to) Tj T*
(have collections made in the churches[237c-1] etc. The next step was) Tj T*
(generally the establishment of public insurance \(_Landes-Assecuranz_\) only) Tj T*
(for houses,[237c-2] but with compulsory membership. This compulsion was) Tj T*
(justified by the continuing interest of the state in the payment of the) Tj T*
(house-tax, as well as by the interest of the eventual owner of the estate,) Tj T*
(and of hypothecation-creditors.[237c-3] [237c-4] The insurance of moveable) Tj T*
(property is much more recent, both by reason of the nature of the property) Tj T*
(itself, which becomes of importance only at a later date, and also on) Tj T*
(account of the much greater difficulty of carrying on such) Tj T*
(insurance.[237c-5] The thought of making this species of insurance) Tj T*
(compulsory, or of turning it over to the state, has seldom been suggested.) Tj T*
