(INFLUENCE OF AN INCREASE OF THE MEANS OF SUBSISTENCE.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The sexual instinct and the love for children are incentives of such) Tj T*
(universality and power, that an increase of the means of subsistence is) Tj T*
(uniformly followed by an increase in the numbers of mankind. _Partout,) Tj T*
(où deux personnes peuvent vivre commodément, il se fait un mariage._) Tj T*
(\(_Montesquieu._\) Thus after a good harvest, the number of marriages and) Tj T*
(births is wont to considerably increase; and conversely to diminish) Tj T*
(after bad harvests.[240-1] [240-2] [240-3] In the former case, it is) Tj T*
(rather hope than actual possession which constitutes the incentive to) Tj T*
(the founding of new families. Hence the greatest increase is not found) Tj T*
(in connection with the absolutely lowest price of corn, but with those) Tj T*
(prices which present the most striking contrast to those of a previous) Tj T*
(bad year.[240-4]) Tj T*
