(In the case of those wild tribes which can only use the forces of nature) Tj T*
(by way of occupation, the small extent of the field of food is filled up) Tj T*
(by even a very sparse population. And the principal means by which) Tj T*
(population is there limited are the following: the overburthening and) Tj T*
(ill treatment of the women,[244-1] by which the simultaneous rearing of) Tj T*
(several small children is rendered impossible;[244-2] the inordinately) Tj T*
(long time that children are kept at the breast;[244-3] the wide-spread) Tj T*
(practice of abortion;[244-4] numerous cases of murder, especially of the) Tj T*
(old and weak;[244-5] everlasting war carried on by hunting nations to) Tj T*
(extend their hunting territory, found in conjunction with cannibalism in) Tj T*
(many tribes.[244-6] Besides, nations of hunters are frequently decimated) Tj T*
(by famine and pestilence, the latter generally a consequence of) Tj T*
(never-ending alternation between gluttony and famine.[244-7]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Most negro nations live in such a state of legal insecurity that it is) Tj T*
(impossible for a higher civilization with its attendant increase of the) Tj T*
(means of subsistence to take root among them. At the same time, their) Tj T*
(sexual impulses are very strong.[244-8] Here the slave-trade constituted) Tj T*
(the chief preventive of over-population. If this traffic were suppressed) Tj T*
(simply and no care taken through the instrumentality of commerce and of) Tj T*
(missions to improve the moral and economical condition of the negroes,) Tj T*
(the only probable but questionable gain would be that the prisoners made) Tj T*
(in the numberless wars generated by famine would be murdered instead of) Tj T*
(being sold.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Nomadic races, with their universal chivalry, are wont to treat their) Tj T*
(women well enough to enable them bear children without any great) Tj T*
(hardship.[244-9] But the mere use of natural pasturage can never be) Tj T*
(carried to great intensity. The transition to agriculture with its) Tj T*
(greater yield of food but with the diminished freedom by which it is) Tj T*
(accompanied is a thing to which these warlike men are so averse that it) Tj T*
(directs the surplus population by the way of emigration into neighboring) Tj T*
(civilized countries, where they either obtain victory, booty and) Tj T*
(supremacy, or are rapidly subjugated. Such migrations are a standing) Tj T*
(chapter in the history of all Asiatic kingdoms; they for a long time) Tj T*
(disturb declining civilized states, finally conquering them, and begin) Tj T*
(the same cycle in the new kingdom.[244-10] Where nomadic races see) Tj T*
(themselves cut off from such migrations their marriages are wont to be) Tj T*
(unfruitful.[244-11]) Tj T*
