(     former the number of years which, on an average, have been) Tj T*
(     accorded to one deceased; by the latter, the number of years) Tj T*
(     after the expiration of which one-half of a given number of) Tj T*
(     human beings have disappeared. If _x_ deceased persons have) Tj T*
(     lived an aggregate of _s_ years, their average duration of) Tj T*
(     life = _s_/_x_. In the case of a whole people, indeed, even) Tj T*
(     the many-years' average of the duration of life of those) Tj T*
(     deceased expresses the true average duration of life only) Tj T*
(     when \(a rare case\) the aggregate population remains) Tj T*
(     stationary. For, when the population is increasing, the) Tj T*
(     average age of the deceased is smaller than the average) Tj T*
(     duration of life, and, when population is decreasing,) Tj T*
(     larger. In the saddest case of all, when there are no births) Tj T*
