(There is found to be in most states, where a decrease in mortality has) Tj T*
(been observed, a diminished number of births likewise.[247-1] This,) Tj T*
(indeed, happens necessarily only in the case in which the means of) Tj T*
(subsistence either do not increase at all, or in a less degree than) Tj T*
(mortality has decreased. Thus, towards the end of the 18th century,) Tj T*
(Norway was the country where the increase and decrease of the population) Tj T*
(were most remarkable for their smallness. There was only one death) Tj T*
(between 1775 and 1784 for every 48 living persons; but, at the same) Tj T*
(time, only one marriage for every 130 living.[247-2] The organization of) Tj T*
(labor was so little developed among the Norwegians, especially in the) Tj T*
(absence of important cities, the industries of which might have been) Tj T*
(able to absorb the surplus population, that almost every one of its) Tj T*
(inhabitants was in a condition to calculate in advance whether or not he) Tj T*
(would have enough to support a family. A person born in the country) Tj T*
(remained generally in his native village all his life. To found a family) Tj T*
(he had either to own a peasant's estate himself or wait until one of the) Tj T*
(day laborer's huts \(_Kathe_\), of which there were several attached to) Tj T*
(each such estate, was vacant. A too large family would certainly have) Tj T*
(died of hunger in the winter time. The clear sober sense of the people) Tj T*
(recognized this fact, and all the farm houses of the peasants were) Tj T*
(without any appreciable injury to morality filled with unmarried) Tj T*
(servants of both sexes who were, indeed, supplied with clothes and food) Tj T*
(but who at the same time were indolent and incapable of) Tj T*
(advancement.[247-3] Where a nation's economy is rapidly advancing, there) Tj T*
(is no necessity why the most natural and when properly directed the most) Tj T*
(beneficent human impulse should be sacrificed to a higher average) Tj T*
(duration of life. But if this must be, when the distribution of the) Tj T*
(national resources is pretty nearly equal, it is not so much the number) Tj T*
(of marriages as the average fruitfulness of marriages that will) Tj T*
(diminish; that is as many persons as before may enter the married state) Tj T*
(but most of them are obliged either to postpone doing so until a later) Tj T*
