(marriages a year.[249-2] In many quarters, where the economic relations) Tj T*
(are very stable, and where peasant estates \(_geschlossene Bauergüter_\)) Tj T*
(are subject to a species of entailing, where consequently the son can) Tj T*
(engage in marriage only after the death of the father, illegitimate) Tj T*
(children are in great part legitimatized by subsequent marriage at a) Tj T*
(later time, and meanwhile brought up in the family of the mother like) Tj T*
(legitimate children.[249-3] Evidently the guilty inconstancy creative of) Tj T*
(ephemeral _liaisons_, and the neglect of the children born of them, do) Tj T*
(not here produce the sad effects which they are wont to in the large) Tj T*
(cities, where illegitimate relations are made and dissolved with) Tj T*
(shocking rapidity. However, births are seldom heard of in the case of) Tj T*
(ruined debauchees.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
