(China is, as a rule, considered the classic land of child-exposure. And) Tj T*
(a writer of the country, who is considered one of the principal) Tj T*
(authorities against the exposure of children, actually claims that it is) Tj T*
(reprehensible only when one has property enough to support them. The) Tj T*
(murder of daughters he especially reprobates as "a struggle against the) Tj T*
(harmony of nature; the more a father performs this act, the more) Tj T*
(daughters are born to him; and no one has ever heard that the birth of) Tj T*
(sons was promoted in this way."[251-6] Moreover, the exposure of) Tj T*
(children in the later periods of antiquity played an important part. In) Tj T*
(Athens, the right of a father to expose his child was recognized by law.) Tj T*
(Even a Socrates accounts it one of the occasional duties of midwives to) Tj T*
(expose children.[251-7] Considered from a moral point of view, Aristotle) Tj T*
(has nothing to say against abortion.[251-8] In Rome, a very ancient law,) Tj T*
(which was still in existence in 475 before Christ, made it the duty of) Tj T*
(every citizen to have and to bring up children.[251-9] It was very) Tj T*
(different in the time of the emperors,[251-10] and until Christianity,) Tj T*
(made the religion of the state, caused a legal prohibition against the) Tj T*
(exposure of children to be passed.[251-11] [251-12]) Tj T*
