(E. It is the indispensable condition precedent of all the measures which) Tj T*
(we have examined, if they would attain their end, that the means of) Tj T*
(subsistence of the people should be increased or at least more equally) Tj T*
(divided among them. Where this has been done the increase of population) Tj T*
(will, as a rule, take care of itself; where it has not, the artificially) Tj T*
(increased procreation of children can only produce new victims for the) Tj T*
(angel of death. A merely more equable distribution can, however, improve) Tj T*
(the condition of the people only in exceedingly rare cases. \(§ 204\). As) Tj T*
(a rule, the diseases which it is attempted to thus cure grow worse, or) Tj T*
(they at least increase in extent. \(§ 80, ff., 250.\) It is quite) Tj T*
(different, of course, when the more equable distribution coincides with) Tj T*
(an absolute growth of the nation's economy. We shall see, later, that,) Tj T*
(for instance, the freedom of land alienation and of industrial pursuits,) Tj T*
(when not accompanied by an important advance in the corresponding) Tj T*
(branches of economy may do more harm than good; but that under favorable) Tj T*
(circumstances a multitude of dormant forces are thereby awakened, and) Tj T*
(that then the national-economical dividend may be increased much more) Tj T*
