(A. The means which consists in rendering marriage less easy by) Tj T*
(legislation is surrounded with peculiar difficulties in densely) Tj T*
(populated countries, which are always highly civilized. The state would) Tj T*
(have here to swim against the stream, and it would be generally a much) Tj T*
(less difficult task to enlarge the field of food. If there remained from) Tj T*
(a former period any inducements held out to promote marriage, it is self) Tj T*
(evident that they should now be discontinued. A voluntary bachelor must) Tj T*
(now no longer be considered as a man who permits one more woman to) Tj T*
(become an old maid, but as one who facilitates marriage to another) Tj T*
(couple.[258-1] On the other hand, it should not be forgotten that, for) Tj T*
(men, generally, marriage is not only an occasion of increased outlay,) Tj T*
(but also an incentive to increased activity and greater economy.[258-2]) Tj T*
(Many states have endeavored to condition the founding of a family by) Tj T*
(requiring evidence that the father has a prospect of being able to) Tj T*
(support one.[258-3] Distinguished theorizers accede to this condition,) Tj T*
(inasmuch as they deny the right of over-population.[258-4] But,) Tj T*
(unfortunately, it is impossible, except in a few extreme cases, to) Tj T*
(assert or deny a prospect of being able to support a family.[258-5] How) Tj T*
(easily is the most remunerative power of labor destroyed by physical or) Tj T*
(mental disease. Scarcely less subject to change is the so-called certain) Tj T*
(opportunity of acquisition afforded by a profession or a trade, when it) Tj T*
(is not guarantied by the possession of considerable capital or of landed) Tj T*
(property, or by some legal privilege. The amount of property required by) Tj T*
(many laws is so small that it alone would suffice to support the family) Tj T*
(only for a few years.[258-6] And yet it has been generally provided that) Tj T*
(the proof of such a property gave one an unconditional right to) Tj T*
(establish a domicile and to marry. It is only where this is wanting that) Tj T*
(special consent is required. But who shall exercise this right of) Tj T*
(consent? The parish, perhaps, because on it the impoverished family) Tj T*
(would fall as a burthen. But it is to be feared that the course of) Tj T*
(procedure here would be too severe. Local narrow-heartedness might) Tj T*
(refuse the right of domicile to skillful and industrious candidates, who) Tj T*
(are in the best situation to maintain a family, but whose competition) Tj T*
(the older members of the parish might dread.[258-7] Hence, in most) Tj T*
(countries, the parish is treated as a party, on whose protest against) Tj T*
(the marriage the state itself decides[258-8] If the state authorities) Tj T*
