(All these dangers disappear when the portion of the nation which has) Tj T*
(emigrated continues economically connected with the body of the nation) Tj T*
(remaining at home. \(Colonizing emigration.\) Here emigration not only) Tj T*
(provides "elbow room" in the mother country, but there arises at the) Tj T*
(same time an increased demand for manufactured articles, an increased) Tj T*
(supply of raw material, by means of which an absolute growth of) Tj T*
(population is made possible.[260-1] England has hitherto enjoyed these) Tj T*
(advantages to the fullest extent, Germany scarcely at all. German) Tj T*
(emigrants to Russia, America, Australia, or Algiers, were, together with) Tj T*
(all they have and are, for the most part lost to their fatherland. They) Tj T*
(become the customers and suppliers of foreign countries, and frequently) Tj T*
(enough the competitors and even enemies of Germany.[260-2] [260-3]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(It might be very different if the stream of German emigration was) Tj T*
(directed towards German colonies for instance, as happened in later) Tj T*
(medieval times, towards the fertile but thinly populated parts of) Tj T*
(Hungary, towards the provinces of Austria and Prussia; perhaps, as List) Tj T*
(wished, towards those parts of Turkey which, God willing, shall yet) Tj T*
(constitute the inheritance of the German people. Thus, through the) Tj T*
(instrumentality of emigration, might a new Germany arise, which would) Tj T*
(directly or indirectly and necessarily ally itself to the old,) Tj T*
(politically, and at the same time constitute the surest bulwark against) Tj T*
(the danger from Slavic power.) Tj T*
