() Tj T*
(The usual error into which the builders of such history fall, is that) Tj T*
(they consider the peculiarities of certain stages of civilization, which) Tj T*
(may be shown to exist among all nations in the corresponding period of) Tj T*
(their history as the national peculiarity of the single people with) Tj T*
(whose history they are, for the time being, concerned. They deduce) Tj T*
(wonderful consequences, from the premises they laid down, but which our) Tj T*
(increasing acquaintance with other nations immediately shows to be) Tj T*
(unfounded.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(There is, however, a number of facts really peculiar to a people which) Tj T*
(make up the national character, and which may give to an observer) Tj T*
(endowed with an imaginative mind, an inkling to the special vocation in) Tj T*
(the economy of providence of a particular people. That a positive system) Tj T*
(can be constructed from the material of such facts, I do not, indeed,) Tj T*
(think. But they are at least a safeguard against false systems, against) Tj T*
(the improper application of analogies, against the idle, fatalistic) Tj T*
(exaggeration of the maxim: "nothing new under the sun!" It had almost) Tj T*
(become the fashion to compare our present with the period of decline of) Tj T*
(the Greek and Roman republics. Frightful parallel, in which the greatest) Tj T*
(and most undoubted differences were frequently overlooked for smaller) Tj T*
(and certainly questionable similarities. Is not the abolition of) Tj T*
(slavery, which has been accomplished among all the most important) Tj T*
(nations of the present, something new and of great import from a moral) Tj T*
(and economic point of view?[265-2] Can the national wealth, which) Tj T*
(depends on labor and frugality, be in any way compared with that which) Tj T*
(was based on plunder? And so, no one can calculate the benefits which) Tj T*
(may be reaped by posterity from the mere continuation of the scientific) Tj T*
(and especially natural-philosophical results obtained by former) Tj T*
(generations. The discovery of the whole earth soon to be completed, and) Tj T*
