(Simultaneously with this opposition, the theory of the international) Tj T*
(balance of trade underwent important refinements, a new and improved) Tj T*
(edition, so to speak, of old Colbertism.[A2-3-1] Each school is wont to) Tj T*
(estimate the favorableness of the balance according to the preponderance) Tj T*
(of that which they consider the most important element in a nation's) Tj T*
(economy. Thus the population-enthusiasts, after the middle of the 18th) Tj T*
(century, distinguished the "balance of advantage" from the "merely) Tj T*
(numerical:" the former is favorable to the country which, by means of) Tj T*
(its exports, employs and feeds the greatest number of men; the latter to) Tj T*
(the country with a preponderating importation of money. And they call) Tj T*
(the former much more important than the latter.[A2-3-2] The great) Tj T*
(advance which this view constitutes over the old system lies chiefly in) Tj T*
(two points: that the number and employment of men are evidently, so far) Tj T*
(as the whole national economy and national life are concerned, a much) Tj T*
(more important element than the quantity of money in a country; and) Tj T*
(further, that now, at least, the possibility of a simultaneous profit on) Tj T*
(both sides is admitted.[A2-3-3] The best writer in this direction, Jos.) Tj T*
(Tucker, is among the great-grand-parents of the Manchester theory of) Tj T*
(to-day!) Tj T*
() Tj T*
