(greater value than those sacrifices. Who would say that the cheapest) Tj T*
(education is always the most advantageous?[A3-4-1] Only by the) Tj T*
(development of industry also, does the nation's economy become) Tj T*
(mature.[A3-4-2] The merely agricultural state can attain neither to the) Tj T*
(same population nor the same energy of capital, to say nothing of the) Tj T*
(same skillfulness of labor, as the mixed agricultural and industrial) Tj T*
(state; nor can it employ its natural forces so completely to) Tj T*
(advantage.[A3-4-3] How many beds of coal, waterfalls, hours of) Tj T*
(leisure,[A3-4-4] and how much aptitude for the arts of industry, can be) Tj T*
(turned to scarcely any account in a merely agricultural state? If,) Tj T*
(therefore, the protective system could materially promote a national) Tj T*
