(All rational education keeps in view as its object, the subsequent) Tj T*
(independence of the pupil. If it desired to continue its guardianship,) Tj T*
(the payment of fees, etc., until an advanced age, it would thereby) Tj T*
(demonstrate either the pupil's want of capacity or the absurdity of its) Tj T*
(methods. The industrial protective system also can be justified as an) Tj T*
(educational measure only on the assumption that it may be gradually) Tj T*
(dispensed with; that is, that, by its means, there may be a prospect of) Tj T*
(attaining to freedom of trade.[A3-7-1] In the case of all highly) Tj T*
(civilized nations, the presumption is in favor of freedom of trade, both) Tj T*
(at home and abroad, and in such nations, the desire for a protective) Tj T*
(system must be looked upon as a symptom of disease.[A3-7-2] [A3-7-3] It) Tj T*
(is true, that recently the inferiority of young countries, even when) Tj T*
(inhabited by a very active and highly educated people, is greatly) Tj T*
(enhanced by the improvement of the means of communication. But this is) Tj T*
(richly compensated for by the simultaneous instinct towards emigration,) Tj T*
(both of capital and workmen from over-full, highly industrial countries;) Tj T*
(whereas, the prohibitions by the state, that extreme of exportation) Tj T*
(embargoes, formerly so frequently resorted to, it is no longer possible) Tj T*
(to carry out.[A3-7-4] [A3-7-5] Now the young country has the advantage of) Tj T*
(being able immediately to use the newest processes of labor, etc.,) Tj T*
(without being hindered by the existence there of earlier imperfect) Tj T*
(apparatus. It is certain that international freedom of trade must be of) Tj T*
(advantage to a people's nationality the moment they have attained to the) Tj T*
(maturity of manhood, for the reason that they are thereby forced to make) Tj T*
(the most of that which is peculiar to them. Care must be taken not to) Tj T*
(confound many-sidedness with all-sidedness.[A3-7-6] The best "protection) Tj T*
(of national labor" might consist in this, that all products should be) Tj T*
(really individually characteristic \(artistic\), all individuals really) Tj T*
(national, and national also in their tastes as consumers. This ideal has) Tj T*
(been pretty closely approximated to by the French in respect to) Tj T*
(fashionable commodities, so that they will hardly purchase such from) Tj T*
(abroad, even without a protective tariff; and the cultured of most) Tj T*
(nations in respect to works of art. Here, too, it is worth considering,) Tj T*
