(INDUSTRIAL-PROTECTIVE POLICY IN PARTICULAR.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(If it be once established generally that an industry is to be) Tj T*
(artificially promoted, and if there be question only of a choice between) Tj T*
(the different measures to be adopted to thus promote it,) Tj T*
(moderate[A3-8-1] import duties are not only the most equable, least) Tj T*
(subject to abuse, but also attended by the greatest number of secondary) Tj T*
(advantages. Here the sacrifice is imposed on all the consumers of the) Tj T*
("protected" commodity, that is, on the entire people, to the extent that) Tj T*
(they come in contact with the commodity in question. Export duties on) Tj T*
(raw materials, on the other hand, compel one single class of the people) Tj T*
(to make sacrifices in order to advance the favored industry.[A3-8-2]) Tj T*
(Export premiums for commodities on which labor has been expended are) Tj T*
(distinguished from import duties as the offensive from the defensive:) Tj T*
(the former promote the artificial trade, the trade which has gone beyond) Tj T*
(its natural basis, the latter curtail it.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Premiums, advances without interest, gifts of machinery etc., to persons) Tj T*
(engaged in industry would operate very usefully under an omniscient) Tj T*
(government.[A3-8-3] But they generally fall to the lot not of the most) Tj T*
(skillful manufacturers, but of the most acceptable supplicants, who now) Tj T*
(are doubly dangerous to the former as competitors.[A3-8-4] The same is) Tj T*
(true to a still greater extent of monopolies granted to undertakings) Tj T*
(which it is intended to promote.[A3-8-5] They require, at least, to be) Tj T*
(vigilantly superintended in case of sale from one person to another;) Tj T*
(otherwise the individual to whom they were first granted is very apt to) Tj T*
(withdraw with the capitalized value of the privilege accorded, and his) Tj T*
(successors, loaded with a heavy debt in the nature of a mortgage, to) Tj T*
(derive no advantage from it.[A3-8-6]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Further, import duties, besides the fiscal advantage which they afford,) Tj T*
(have the police advantage that they may, like quarantine provisions,) Tj T*
(prevent somewhat the inroads of many economic diseases: thus, for) Tj T*
(instance, gluts of the market, and still more, the severe chronic) Tj T*
(disease of ruinously low wages.[A3-8-7] But only very moderate hopes) Tj T*
(from protective duties should be entertained in all such respects as) Tj T*
(these.[A3-8-8]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Prohibition proper operates, as a rule, very disastrously.[A3-8-9] It) Tj T*
(spoils those engaged in industry by a feeling of too great security) Tj T*
(\(mortals' chiefest enemy: Shakespeare\). It may even lead to complete) Tj T*
(monopoly, when the industry requires very large means and the country is) Tj T*
(small. The inducement to smuggling is peculiarly great here. But even) Tj T*
(duties, so high that they far exceed the insurance premium of smuggling,) Tj T*
(can be of very little advantage either to industry or to the exchequer.) Tj T*
(They can only promote the smuggling trade. However, the repeal of an) Tj T*
(import prohibition or the abolition of a tariff approaching to a) Tj T*
(prohibition should be announced long enough in advance to enable the) Tj T*
(capital invested in the protected industry to be withdrawn without too) Tj T*
(heavy a loss.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
